## 7. Risks and Mitigations

| Risk | Impact | Mitigation |
|------|--------|------------|
| Design iteration expands scope | Delays delivery | Agree on a fixed set of admin screens and one revision round |
| AI-generated code has inconsistent patterns | Harder to maintain | Refactor pass during QA, add linting and formatting rules |
| Security gaps in admin or uploads | Data exposure | Dedicated security checklist in Phase 2 |
| Client unfamiliar with admin tools | Support burden after launch | Admin guide plus recorded walkthrough |
| Third-party service limits or costs | Unexpected bills or outages | Document plan tiers and usage limits in handoff notes |

---

## 8. Definition of Done

A task or phase is done when:

- Functionality works as described in this plan
- Code is merged to `main` through a reviewed PR
- No new console errors or failing tests
- UI matches the design system and works at supported widths
- Relevant docs are updated

